[[File:Fighting the Mad Angel.png|thumb|width=300x300|A player fighting the Mad Angel.]]
After completion of [[Fallen From Grace]], the [[Mad Angel]] can be fought again.

==Requirements==
* Completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[Fallen From Grace]]

===Recommendations===
* {{SCP|Attack|75|link=yes}}
* {{SCP|Prayer|43|link=yes}} minimum for [[Protect from Melee]] / [[Protect from Magic]]
* {{SCP|Prayer|70|link=yes}} and {{SCP|Defence|70|link=yes}} for [[Piety]]

==Transportation==
* The fastest route to the cathedral in which the Mad Angel resides is via [[Ardeaglais teleport]].
* Alternatively, use a [[Slayer ring]] to teleport to the cave underneath the boss. Then either interact with the golem to the north and climb the stairs to the boss, or exit the cave to the west and run to the boss.
* You may also use a [[necklace of passage]], then run west and climb the [[Rocks (Wyrmscraig)|rocks]] to reach the front door to the cathedral. This requires you to have mined the rocks at the top of the shortcut, as well as 54 [[Agility]].

==Fight overview==
The Mad Angel attacks primarily with [[melee]], and is weak to [[golembane weapons]]; [[Protect from Melee]] will reduce the max hit of its standard attacks from 31 to 5. After three standard attacks, it will perform a special attack.

Upon reaching 350 Hitpoints (~45%), the Mad Angel will enter the enrage phase at the next available opportunity, denoted by a {{overhead|...!}} overhead message. During this phase, its special attacks are performed quicker, requiring quicker reaction times to counter them. Additionally, it will use all three of its specials consecutively at the start of this phase.

{| class="wikitable align-center-1" style="text-align:left;"
!Attack
!Description
!Demonstration
|-
|Sweep attack
|The Mad Angel stands still, drawing its sword back to either the left or the right. After a few seconds, it will cleave the area towards the side where the player was, as well as the side it drew the sword back from. The boss will perform this cleave 4 times (6 times during the enrage phase). [[Protect from Melee]] will reduce the damage from being caught in this attack by ~50%.

In order to dodge the cleave, the player must run to the side of the boss opposite the sword or behind it. If an attack is successfully dodged to the side (not behind it), the player's next attack will be 100% accurate and damage rolls below 50% of their maximum hit will be raised to 50%.

Players should be mindful to ensure that the boss's tiles are not against a wall, as when it performs a cleave the tiles to dodge may be unreachable. If the boss is against a wall, players can click inside of the boss's 3x3 area, on the middle tile toward the direction the dodge would be successful, to receive the buff and avoid damage.
|[[File:Mad Angel - Sword Cleave dodging.mp4|center|500px]]
|-
|Blast attack
|The Mad Angel launches a ball of light towards a destination tile, indicated with a looming shadow on the floor. If it reaches this destination, it will explode and deal 30+ damage to the entire arena. This explosion's damage can be reduced by ~50% with [[Protect from Magic]], however it is possible for a standard attack to land during the same tick.

Standing on the destination tile will instead bounce the ball of light back to boss, dealing 18-22 damage to it; if done correctly, the ball will be bounced three times every time it performs this attack.

This is the only special attack sequence during which the boss will continue to perform its standard attack. 
|[[File:Mad Angel - Exploding Light.mp4|center|500px]]
|-
|Smite attack
|The Mad Angel brings the sword towards its chest, then begins charging a lightning attack that must be protected from with [[Protect from Magic]]. Simply having the prayer overhead will reduce the damage by ~75%, but activating the prayer at the same tick that the lightning strikes will fully negate the damage, as well as guarantee a [[maximum hit]] for the next attack.

The timing to perfectly negate the attack requires that the player click on Protect from Magic {{ticks|4}} after the attack begins charging, when the blue crackling first becomes visible. Players may also react to a visual cue, by activating the prayer when the boss's wings flap slightly once fully extended. 

During the enrage phase, the boss will perform three strikes. The first attack can be countered normally, with the second strike occurring {{ticks|4}} after the first, and the third occurring {{ticks|2}} after the second.

Another method of negating damage from this attack is to [[Prayer#Prayer flicking|1-tick prayer flick]] Protect from Magic for the duration of the animation. While this method is more click intensive, it does not require the player to time the flick on the exact tick of each attack. This approach works well for both the single attack and the enrage phase triple attack. 
|[[File:Mad Angel - Lightning Smite.mp4|center|500px]]
|}

==Equipment==
Melee is the simplest and most effective way to kill the Mad Angel. Due to its [[golembane]] weakness, a [[granite hammer]] is particularly effective, although many crush weapons are viable. 

Since accuracy is guaranteed when perfectly dodging the sweep attack and max hits are guaranteed on the first hitsplat after perfectly praying against the smite attack, lower tier options perform well and swapping weapons throughout the fight at lower levels may be worthwhile; for example, to utilise boosted accuracy on the [[dual macuahuitl]] but using a higher accuracy weapon at the start of the fight. Most other ranged and magic setups will not perform well due to the boss's defence. However, the [[twisted bow]] can take advantage of the opportunities to hit with guaranteed accuracy.

